# matmul_float16b_lofi_fp32acc.cbtable
#   Fourth cell of the 2x2 (fidelity x DST accumulator width) design used to explain the
#   docs/tt_bringup_log.md §16.3 inversion. See matmul_float16b_lofi.cbtable and
#   matmul_float16b_fp32acc.cbtable for the other two off-diagonal cells; the shipped
#   matmul_float16b.cbtable (HiFi4, dst_accum_mode 0) is the fourth.
#
#   If DST accumulator width is the dominant error term and fidelity is secondary, this
#   cell should land close to matmul_float16b_fp32acc.cbtable's accuracy on the long-K
#   shapes (both 32-bit-accumulator arms converge, regardless of fidelity) rather than
#   close to matmul_float16b_lofi.cbtable's (which would mean fidelity, not accumulator
#   width, still dominates even with the accumulator widened).
#
#   NEVER pointed to by build_tensix_program.sh in Makefile.ops or any shipped program
#   directory. It exists only for foundry/tt/tests/test_fidelity_sweep.c.
#
#   Format: tools/emit_tensix_cb_formats.py

math_fidelity  0
approx         0
dst_accum_mode 1

cb  0  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb  1  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb 16  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
